    "narrative": "Our offense looks primed for a productive day against a slate of vulnerable arms, headlined by **Daulton Varsho** (69.56) and **Taylor Ward** (68.88). **Daulton Varsho** earns the top spot in the lineup due to a high-upside matchup against M\u00e1rquez, whose 5.58 xERA provides the most favorable environment of the day. Meanwhile, **Taylor Ward** and **Dylan Beavers** (68.38) benefit significantly from park factors and a plus-matchup against Lugo. While **Dylan Beavers** faces a slight efficiency drag due to the opposing pitcher\u2019s elite hold on the running game, his overall projection remains high enough to warrant a start. **Luis Arraez** (65.86) and **Jung Hoo Lee** (62.57) are also strong plays, as both capitalize on the favorable 4.72 xERA of Lorenzen, with **Luis Arraez** getting a massive 18% boost in his projection from the favorable SP skill matchup.\n\nThe most difficult roster decision today was benching **Bryce Harper**, who remains a high-floor talent but struggles to crack the starting nine due to a brutal draw against an elite arm in Skubal (2.69 xERA). The optimizer favored the cumulative efficiency of the other spots, particularly with players like **Jung Hoo Lee** and **Daulton Varsho** seeing massive platoon and matchup-based score surges that **Bryce Harper** could not overcome given the -19% SP skill penalty. Similarly, **Drew Gilbert** (51.55) looked tempting, but his bottom-of-the-order assignment (8th) created a drag on his run-production potential that kept him on the pine in favor of the higher-scoring options currently in play.\n\nRisk management remains a priority given the scarcity of stolen bases. We are carefully monitoring **Tyler Freeman** (49.94); while he resides in the bottom of the order, he is a primary \"green light\" candidate today against McDonald, whose slow delivery allows us to chase those critical SB points despite a mediocre overall efficiency score. Conversely, we are keeping a close eye on **Cal Raleigh** (52.07), whose projection is weighed down by a tough matchup against Seymour. Should the weather or last-minute lineup shifts prove volatile, we have sufficient depth on the bench\u2014including **Gavin Sheets** and **Ryan Waldschmidt**\u2014to pivot, though we are currently comfortable with the calculated risks taken in this rotation.",
